From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:26:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bridge: carry the message timestamp in milliseconds as well

Upstream now hands the C side the message time in seconds only
(aa572d5). Signal identifies a message by its sent timestamp in
milliseconds: quotes and reactions target it, and receipts report it.
Converting to seconds loses that id.

Add a timestamp_ms field next to timestamp_seconds in the bridge Message
(Rust and C). Fill it from the envelope timestamp for incoming messages,
and with the current time in ms where the backend makes up a message
itself (send feedback, errors), as the bridge did before aa572d5. Pass
it through presage_handle_text() and presage_handle_attachment(), and
keep it in XferData for attachments. Nothing uses it yet; the reaction,
reply and receipt patches that follow do.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
